        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `/thinking high|low|medium` was rejected with \"not supported for github-copilot/claude-sonnet-4.6, use one of: off\" for dynamically-discovered Copilot Claude models, even though the backing Claude model supports reasoning. Only `off` was advertised.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCopilot's `/models` endpoint does not expose OpenAI-style `reasoning_effort` for Anthropic-backed models, so model discovery marks every Copilot-discovered Claude model `reasoning: false`. The shared thinking resolver (`src/auto-reply/thinking.ts`) then discarded github-copilot's declared level set and fell back to off-only, because neither thinking surface set `preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse`. This PR sets that flag for Claude models (detected via the existing `anthropic-messages` transport signal) on BOTH github-copilot thinking surfaces, mirroring `anthropic`, `amazon-bedrock`, `google`, and `moonshot`:\n- the active provider hook (`resolveThinkingProfile` in `index.ts`), and\n- the bundled provider-policy surface (`provider-policy-api.ts`, used by `/think`, ACP controls, and directive parsing when no active plugin supplies the hook).\n\nThis preserves the levels the hooks already declare (`off/minimal/low/medium/high`) and invents no new ones; non-Claude Copilot models without `reasoning_effort` stay off-only.\n\nPer review on #99240: both thinking surfaces must agree before merge.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers running Copilot-routed Claude models (e.g. `claude-sonnet-4.6`, `claude-opus-4.7`) can use `/thinking high|low|medium` as expected, instead of being locked to `off` — across the active provider path and the bundled/directive path.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `extensions/github-copilot/index.test.ts`: a Claude model resolves `preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse: true` with the `[off,minimal,low,medium,high]` level set; a non-Claude model (`gpt-5.4-mini`) leaves the flag unset.\n- `extensions/github-copilot/provider-policy-api.test.ts`: the same assertions for the bundled policy surface (Claude → flag set; non-Claude → unset) — 11/11 pass.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-providers.config.ts extensions/github-copilot`: thinking tests pass. The full github-copilot suite only has pre-existing Windows `EBUSY` SQLite-teardown flakes in token-onboarding tests, unrelated to this change.\n\nLive end-to-end Copilot proof (a real `/thinking high` round-trip) still requires a maintainer with Copilot credentials; the code fix is complete on both surfaces and covered by the unit tests above.\n\n🤖 AI-assisted. Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code).\n\nCloses #99240",
        "branch": "claude/99240-copilot-thinking-levels",
